  "verdict": "CENTRE-BIAS CONFIRMED AND QUANTIFIED, AND IT WAS PROPPING UP THE MANIFOLD'S ONLY LEAD. The trivial centre-prior baseline scores 22/22 (1.00) under the centred window used by every localization run to date, and 0/22 (0.00) once the transition is moved off-centre -- a drop of 1.00 (>= 0.30, so the inflation \u00a72b warns about is real). So the ABSOLUTE localization hit rates reported across the suite were inflated by the symmetric-window construction and must be read as such. Centred, H1 had the manifold ahead 14/22 vs 9/22; with the transition off-centre the comparison is a DEAD TIE: manifold 10/22 vs scalar 10/22 (McNemar manifold-only 5, scalar-only 5, p = 1.000). The pre-registered paired verdict did not flip (not significant either way), but the honest reading is not that H1 'survives': the manifold's small centred lead was in good part a centring artefact, and on the cleanest test available the geometry adds NOTHING over a one-line scalar band-power CUSUM. The update runs against the manifold -- it lowers, rather than leaves neutral, the prior for a properly powered rematch. Not a power increase: n is unchanged from H1 (downloads blocked in this session by an environment-side egress-TLS failure for the data hosts, not a PhysioNet outage).",
